WEBVTT

00:02.502 --> 00:05.938
<i>[Singing] It seems today that all you see</i>

00:06.039 --> 00:09.236
<i>Is violence in movies and sex on TV</i>

00:09.342 --> 00:12.800
<i>But where are those
good old-fashioned values</i>

00:12.912 --> 00:15.437
<i>On which we used to rely?</i>

00:15.882 --> 00:19.215
<i>Lucky there's a family guy</i>

00:19.319 --> 00:22.618
<i>Lucky there's a man who
positively can do</i>

00:22.722 --> 00:24.622
<i>All the things that make us</i>

00:24.724 --> 00:25.986
<i>Laugh and cry</i>

00:26.092 --> 00:30.552
<i>He's a family guy</i>

00:35.335 --> 00:36.666
[People laughing]

00:36.770 --> 00:39.933
This is ridiculous.
Why did y'all drag me here?

00:40.040 --> 00:42.941
Because you can't just
sit home every night since Loretta left.

00:43.043 --> 00:44.772
You got to get out and meet some women.

00:44.878 --> 00:47.176
Well, I suppose I could give it a try.

00:47.747 --> 00:51.444
Hey, baby. How'd you like to go black
and then have to make...

00:51.551 --> 00:54.952
a difficult decision regarding
whether or not to go back?

00:55.055 --> 00:58.024
Sorry, I went burnt sienna
and I never went back.

00:58.124 --> 01:00.319
Ready, baby? Who's this clown?

01:04.731 --> 01:08.929
Open up, Stewie.
The airplane's coming in for a landing.

01:09.702 --> 01:12.762
I guess the pilot must have been
JFK Junior.

01:13.039 --> 01:15.439
Even I found that to be in bad taste.

01:15.542 --> 01:17.100
Hi, Mom. Hi, Dad.

01:17.210 --> 01:20.577
Good morning, Chris. Oh, my God!
Look at the size of that pimple.

01:20.680 --> 01:22.739
You're like a circus freak!

01:23.283 --> 01:25.751
I'm kidding.
You're just becoming a man, sweetie.

01:25.852 --> 01:27.843
Yeah. I remember when I became a man.

01:28.088 --> 01:31.751
The operation was a success.
What are you gonna go by now?

01:31.858 --> 01:33.120
Peter.

01:33.226 --> 01:35.820
You know, Chris, we'll have to
do something about that.

01:35.929 --> 01:37.829
But I don't wanna get rid of my zit.

01:37.931 --> 01:41.196
I like him. He's my friend.
His name is Doug.

01:41.301 --> 01:43.030
I just wish I didn't have to look at it.

01:43.136 --> 01:45.434
We have to look at your anus all day.

01:45.538 --> 01:46.732
Thank you.

01:49.309 --> 01:52.176
<i>The Bachelorette comes to Quahog
in search of male contestants.</i>

01:52.278 --> 01:53.745
<i>Story at 11:00.</i>

01:54.180 --> 01:56.148
<i>Well, actually, that was pretty much it.</i>

01:56.249 --> 01:57.773
<i>But there will be other stuff, too.</i>

01:57.884 --> 01:59.579
<i>Look, I'm turning down the thermostat.</i>

01:59.686 --> 02:01.381
<i>See Diane's erect nipples at 11:00.</i>

02:01.488 --> 02:04.150
<i>Oh, my God!
The Bachelorette is coming to Quahog.</i>

02:04.257 --> 02:06.020
That's, like, my favorite show ever.

02:06.126 --> 02:07.616
Meg, how can you watch that crap?

02:07.727 --> 02:09.592
That show is not reality. It's all staged.

02:09.696 --> 02:11.926
It's a complete mockery
of human relationships.

02:12.031 --> 02:15.125
You know, this could be the perfect way
for Cleveland to meet Mrs. Right.

02:15.235 --> 02:17.635
I got to tell him. Hey, Cleveland.

02:17.837 --> 02:21.796
Joe? Sorry, I dialed the wrong number.
I meant to call Cleveland.

02:21.908 --> 02:24.103
No, I just wanted to tell him something.

02:24.210 --> 02:26.906
No, I'd like to talk to you, too.
It's just that...

02:27.013 --> 02:29.743
Fine. I'll call you after I talk to Cleveland.

02:29.849 --> 02:32.249
I don't feel obligated. I want to.

02:33.353 --> 02:35.753
You're a good pimple, Doug.

02:35.855 --> 02:37.152
Feed me.

02:37.790 --> 02:39.485
You can talk?

02:39.592 --> 02:42.060
That's right.
And we're gonna raise some hell.

02:42.162 --> 02:44.221
All right! Raise some hell!

03:10.456 --> 03:13.254
<i>So, why would you be a good candidate
on The Bachelorette?</i>

03:13.359 --> 03:15.486
I would be perfect for your show...

03:15.595 --> 03:18.894
because I know
how to talk dirty to the ladies.

03:18.998 --> 03:23.264
Oh, yes. Oh, yes. That feels so good.

03:23.369 --> 03:25.394
Spit in my mouth.

03:27.240 --> 03:29.367
Two hundred auditions and nothing.

03:29.475 --> 03:30.874
We still got one guy waiting.

03:30.977 --> 03:33.946
You lined up 201 auditions?
What a weird number.

03:34.047 --> 03:35.014
You're weird.

03:35.315 --> 03:38.716
Peter, I can't do this.
I am too nervous. I got to go.

03:38.818 --> 03:40.843
No, Cleveland,
I'm not gonna let you do this.

03:40.954 --> 03:42.444
I'll tie you down, if I have to.

03:43.623 --> 03:45.853
Peter, this is only making it worse.

03:45.959 --> 03:48.587
Oh, God, my claustrophobia is setting in.

03:48.695 --> 03:50.856
It's all right. It's okay. It's the fabric.

03:50.964 --> 03:53.432
It's your clothes. Let's get your clothes off.

03:53.533 --> 03:56.331
Peter, what's wrong with you? I am naked!

03:56.436 --> 03:58.597
Oh, God, you're self-conscious. I'm sorry.

03:58.705 --> 04:00.536
Here. You know what?
Look, Cleveland, look.

04:00.640 --> 04:02.301
See? Now you're not alone, Cleveland.

04:02.408 --> 04:05.400
Let me out of here!
I need to get out of here.

04:05.511 --> 04:09.413
Cleveland, no, you're staying.
This is for your own good.

04:09.882 --> 04:11.213
Oh, my God!

04:13.453 --> 04:15.444
Hi, we're here for the interview.

04:17.624 --> 04:21.151
Excuse me. Hi. Listen, I just wanted
to apologize for Peter.

04:21.261 --> 04:23.491
He was just trying to help out his friend.

04:23.596 --> 04:26.326
You see, his wife left him
and he's been kind of Ionely...

04:26.432 --> 04:28.229
confused about what he really wants.

04:28.334 --> 04:29.824
- What's your name?
- Brian.

04:29.936 --> 04:33.633
<i>Congratulations, Brian.
You're gonna be on The Bachelorette.</i>

04:33.740 --> 04:36.709
Really? You're sure
you don't want to reconsider my friend?

04:36.809 --> 04:38.470
Let me see.

04:39.012 --> 04:40.980
Oh, that ain't bad!

04:45.885 --> 04:49.048
<i>Brian, I can't believe
you're gonna be on The Bachelorette.</i>

04:49.155 --> 04:51.180
Yeah, I thought you said
those shows were stupid.

04:51.291 --> 04:52.258
They are stupid.

04:52.358 --> 04:54.826
But I figured I got a few days
of free booze and food...

04:54.927 --> 04:56.895
before they kick me off.
I could use a vacation.

04:56.996 --> 05:00.659
Oh, yeah, because you've got
such a heavy workload around here.

05:02.068 --> 05:05.265
How you coming on that novel
you're working on, huh?

05:05.638 --> 05:08.300
Got a big stack of papers there?

05:09.108 --> 05:12.441
Got a nice little story
you working on there?

05:12.545 --> 05:15.878
The big novel you've been working on
for three years, huh?

05:16.716 --> 05:19.116
Got a compelling protagonist?

05:19.218 --> 05:21.743
Got an obstacle for him to overcome?

05:23.122 --> 05:25.215
Little story brewing there? Working on?

05:25.792 --> 05:28.090
Working on that for quite some time, huh?

05:28.194 --> 05:32.255
Talking about that three years ago.
Been working on that the whole time?

05:32.365 --> 05:35.391
Nice little narrative.
Beginning, middle, and end.

05:35.501 --> 05:38.732
Some friends become enemies,
some enemies become friends?

05:38.838 --> 05:42.569
At the end your main character
is richer for the experience? Yeah?

05:44.010 --> 05:46.240
No, you deserve some time off.

05:47.947 --> 05:50.313
I am super excited.
You think she'll be hot?

05:50.416 --> 05:52.611
- I bet she'll be hot.
- I think she'll be hot, too.

05:52.719 --> 05:54.277
No way! So do I!

05:57.123 --> 05:59.057
- Quagmire.
- Hey, Brian!

05:59.158 --> 06:02.059
- How did you get on the show?
- I had to do a few favors.

06:02.161 --> 06:04.629
I got to get on that show.
Come on, I'll do anything.

06:04.731 --> 06:05.925
Anything?

06:06.733 --> 06:09.031
- Yeah.
- All right.

06:10.203 --> 06:11.431
- Okay, you're ready?
- Yep.

06:11.537 --> 06:13.334
Okay, check under the bed.

06:13.439 --> 06:15.805
- No, nothing.
- Check in the closet.

06:15.908 --> 06:17.603
No, no monsters in here.

06:17.710 --> 06:19.109
Now check the bathroom.

06:19.212 --> 06:21.146
- No, none in here, either.
- Okay, good.

06:21.247 --> 06:24.045
<i>- So, can I be on The Bachelorette?
- Yeah. Goodnight.</i>

06:26.819 --> 06:29.049
Peter, I'm getting
a little worried about Chris.

06:29.155 --> 06:32.215
All he does lately is sit alone in his room
talking to that zit.

06:32.325 --> 06:34.088
Relax, Lois. What's a zit gonna do?

06:34.193 --> 06:37.390
Talk to him and tell him to
sneak out of the house and cause trouble?

06:39.132 --> 06:42.329
Now light it, ring the doorbell,
and run like hell!

06:42.435 --> 06:44.995
- I don't know about this, Doug.
- Just do it!

06:48.474 --> 06:49.702
Oh, good Lord!

06:54.213 --> 06:56.443
Is that... Doody!

06:56.549 --> 06:59.848
I'm doing the dishes, Joe.
I'll change you in a minute.

07:04.290 --> 07:07.259
Trevor, this is Brooke, the bachelorette.

07:07.460 --> 07:09.325
I wasn't too nervous.
When I am nervous I work out.

07:10.496 --> 07:12.521
I wasn't working out,
so I must not have been nervous.

07:12.832 --> 07:14.299
I was very pleased and surprised.

07:15.535 --> 07:18.003
I really was not expecting an open bar.

07:18.104 --> 07:20.072
Top-shelf booze, I tell you.

07:20.173 --> 07:23.142
And this guy knew his stuff.
Made me a Mojito.

07:25.578 --> 07:27.876
I don't think it's a gay drink.

07:28.080 --> 07:30.014
Mojito!

07:31.984 --> 07:34.748
Hey, guys.
Well, it's been great to meet you all.

07:34.854 --> 07:37.880
And I am looking forward
to getting to know you while we're here.

07:40.893 --> 07:43.123
- Dude, put your pants on.
- Shut up.

07:43.329 --> 07:44.921
Well, I really like all the guys.

07:45.031 --> 07:47.625
But some of them
seem a little too competitive.

07:48.801 --> 07:52.567
I got to tell you. I don't know what she
would possibly see in Count Chocula.

07:52.672 --> 07:54.731
I think he's just here
because he's a minority.

08:07.053 --> 08:10.147
You were right, Doug. Mischief is fun.

08:10.256 --> 08:13.157
We're the best pals since the Snorks.

08:13.259 --> 08:15.454
I am having a really great time.

08:15.561 --> 08:18.530
Me, too. I really value our friendship.

08:18.631 --> 08:22.032
You're not like those other Snorks
who only want one thing.

08:22.134 --> 08:25.035
Oh, that was clumsy. Hang on a second.

08:33.279 --> 08:36.510
Gentlemen, it's time
for the first rose ceremony.

08:36.616 --> 08:39.483
Who gets to stay,
and who takes the bus ride home...

08:39.585 --> 08:40.950
it's up to Brooke.

08:41.888 --> 08:44.823
- Trevor.
- That's what Trevor's talking about.

08:45.291 --> 08:47.191
Hey, can I say hi to a friend of mine?

08:47.293 --> 08:49.227
- Sure.
- Hi, Jesus!

08:49.495 --> 08:50.655
No way!

08:50.763 --> 08:51.752
[Phone ringing]

08:51.864 --> 08:53.855
Hello. I know. I saw.

08:54.066 --> 08:55.158
Glenn.

08:59.171 --> 09:02.004
- Brian.
- What? Are you serious?

09:02.108 --> 09:04.042
I feel like I didn't get to know you at all.

09:04.143 --> 09:06.236
- Would you accept this rose?
- All right.

09:06.345 --> 09:09.610
But I think this whole thing is about
as pointless as Peter's cow-kite.

09:14.420 --> 09:18.254
This is never gonna work. Damn cow.
Cleveland, what am I doing wrong?

09:18.357 --> 09:21.952
You got to get her running
before you start running.

09:25.131 --> 09:26.098
Chris.

09:26.432 --> 09:28.764
Chris, honey, can I talk to you?

09:32.004 --> 09:34.029
Oh, my God, he's gone!

09:34.140 --> 09:35.869
That means this room is mine now.

09:35.975 --> 09:37.966
I am gonna party my ass off in here.

09:38.077 --> 09:39.806
Great pot, Stewie.

09:39.912 --> 09:42.073
Yeah, I got it from
our cleaning lady's boyfriend.

09:42.181 --> 09:45.150
It's okay, though, 'cause she's gonna
use the money to get a mammogram.

09:46.118 --> 09:48.586
Chris, where have you been?

09:48.688 --> 09:51.179
Doug told me I don't need to listen to you.

09:51.290 --> 09:53.918
Doug? Your pimple? Oh, that is it!

09:54.026 --> 09:56.859
First thing tomorrow, we're going down
to Goldman's Pharmacy...

09:56.963 --> 09:59.090
and get some astringent
to get rid of that thing.

09:59.198 --> 10:01.564
What did I tell you?
She's trying to drive us apart.

10:01.667 --> 10:03.066
We can't let that happen.

10:04.670 --> 10:06.399
I am in no mood.

10:09.408 --> 10:12.935
Welcome to the Saddleback Ranch
and our first group date.

10:13.045 --> 10:15.206
Is everyone ready
for a little cowboy action?

10:15.314 --> 10:18.112
- Yeah!
- I love horses.

10:18.217 --> 10:20.412
Sorry, I am late, Brian. Here's your ride.

10:20.519 --> 10:22.749
Oh, come on, you can't expect me
to ride that thing.

10:22.855 --> 10:24.652
Sorry, we're short on horses.

10:25.558 --> 10:28.459
You know what? Forget it.
I'll just go smoke.

10:28.961 --> 10:31.225
- Hey, there, Adam.
- Hello, Henry.

10:31.330 --> 10:34.231
I have the power!

10:45.444 --> 10:46.741
Brooke, what are you doing here?

10:46.846 --> 10:48.677
Oh, I just can't take it anymore.

10:48.781 --> 10:51.215
All these guys just coming on to me.

10:51.317 --> 10:54.218
I had to sneak off.
Oh, could I bum one of those?

10:55.388 --> 10:58.152
You know, I don't even know
why I agreed to do this show.

10:58.257 --> 10:59.485
This is just so not me.

10:59.592 --> 11:02.925
I'd much rather just be home
listening to my old jazz records.

11:03.029 --> 11:05.930
Really? I didn't know. I actually have
quite a jazz collection myself.

11:06.032 --> 11:08.557
- What do you like?
- DJ Jazzy Jeff!

11:09.402 --> 11:10.869
I'm kidding!

11:12.104 --> 11:14.299
Oh, you got me. Oh, you got me, yeah.

11:14.407 --> 11:17.899
No, I really like Coleman Hawkins,
Ben Webster.

11:18.010 --> 11:20.877
Oh, and early Coltrane,
before he got clean.

11:20.980 --> 11:22.845
Yeah, no junk, no soul.

11:22.948 --> 11:25.314
No kidding. I mean, look at Chevy Chase.

11:25.951 --> 11:27.179
Right.

11:27.286 --> 11:30.050
You know, I got to say, I thought
she was just some actress...

11:30.156 --> 11:34.354
Iooking for her 15 minutes of fame,
but she's pretty sharp, you know.

11:34.460 --> 11:37.293
I guess you can't judge
a Brooke by her cover.

11:38.597 --> 11:40.690
You can cut that out, right?

11:40.800 --> 11:45.499
And maybe you can cut out when I said
junk earlier, the whole Chevy Chase thing.

11:45.604 --> 11:49.040
Seems like he's probably
the kind of guy who might sue.

11:49.141 --> 11:51.268
I mean, the guy's got to have
no money left.

11:53.079 --> 11:54.341
All right, gentlemen...

11:54.447 --> 11:57.439
let's see how Glenn's
private date with Brooke is going.

11:58.150 --> 12:00.846
Hey, Brooke, what do you say,
we get you some more champagne?

12:00.953 --> 12:02.113
Sure.

12:08.761 --> 12:10.092
All right.

12:13.199 --> 12:15.258
Hey, forgot about you guys.

12:15.367 --> 12:17.392
Well, I guess the date's over.

12:17.503 --> 12:20.370
Goodnight, Brooke.
Thanks for a lovely evening.

12:22.408 --> 12:23.773
[Glenn sniffing]

12:24.643 --> 12:26.201
[Glenn exclaiming in delight]

12:28.080 --> 12:30.708
Oh, my God, Peter,
it looks like there's been a break in.

12:31.984 --> 12:33.542
Do you think so?

12:34.620 --> 12:36.611
Oh, God, they're back.

12:40.326 --> 12:42.260
Whoa, awesome! Totally awesome!

12:43.562 --> 12:45.154
All right, Goldman.

12:45.264 --> 12:47.061
What the hell is your problem, Mort?

12:47.166 --> 12:50.158
I am sorry, Peter. I thought you were
one of those criminals...

12:50.269 --> 12:54.103
who broke in and destroyed
my entire stock of acne medication.

12:54.206 --> 12:57.004
Oh, my God. Peter, do you think
Chris might have done this?

12:57.109 --> 13:00.442
Come on, Lois, he doesn't have the wild
streak you had when you were younger.

13:00.546 --> 13:04.004
For God's sake, you used to make
Plasto molds of celebrity body parts.

13:05.751 --> 13:08.049
Okay, Daryl, it's almost dry.

13:08.154 --> 13:09.781
Very nice, by the way.

13:09.889 --> 13:12.585
This one's going on the shelf
right next to Dan Fogelberg.

13:12.691 --> 13:14.318
Hey, Lois, am I up next?

13:14.426 --> 13:17.987
Just wait in your dressing room.
I'll come back for you, Oates.

13:18.097 --> 13:20.031
I am not coming back for Oates.

13:22.101 --> 13:24.194
Glenn, will you accept this rose?

13:24.303 --> 13:25.463
Really? After I drugged you...

13:25.571 --> 13:27.698
and tried to have sex
with your unconscious body?

13:27.807 --> 13:28.774
- What?
- Yes.

13:28.874 --> 13:31.274
This is the final rose tonight.

13:34.246 --> 13:35.838
- Brian.
- Yes!

13:35.948 --> 13:38.212
Yeah, I mean,
I know I was skeptical at first...

13:38.317 --> 13:42.219
but I got to be honest, I've never
felt this way about anyone before.

13:42.321 --> 13:45.484
I mean, I am in love. That's it.

13:46.258 --> 13:47.589
I am in love.

13:48.093 --> 13:51.085
I finally understand
those songs on the radio.

13:51.630 --> 13:54.394
<i>[Singing] What did you think</i>

13:55.334 --> 13:58.633
<i>I would do at this moment</i>

13:59.238 --> 14:02.537
<i>When you're standing before me</i>

14:02.741 --> 14:05.608
<i>With tears in your eyes</i>

14:07.780 --> 14:11.045
Brooke has narrowed her choice down
to Quagmire and Brian.

14:11.150 --> 14:13.948
All that's left is for Brooke
to meet their families.

14:19.792 --> 14:22.693
Hey, Brian, I can't wait
to meet your family.

14:22.795 --> 14:25.093
Yeah, me, too. They're pretty great.

14:25.197 --> 14:28.064
Brian, welcome home, you son of a bitch!

14:28.167 --> 14:30.601
So, did you loose?
You got to tell me all about it.

14:30.703 --> 14:32.603
Hey, how was your bachelorette?

14:32.705 --> 14:35.333
Was she a dumb bimbo like you said
but with a big rack.

14:35.441 --> 14:37.033
Come on in and tell me everything.

14:37.142 --> 14:40.873
I bet your stories will make me laugh
so hard, I'll shoot milk out of my nose.

14:40.980 --> 14:42.914
Peter, this is Brooke, the bachelorette.

14:43.015 --> 14:44.744
She's having dinner with us tonight.

14:44.850 --> 14:47.751
I went over this with you
a few minutes ago.

14:50.289 --> 14:53.747
Why, it's wonderful to meet you.
We've heard so many nice things.

14:53.859 --> 14:56.623
Yes, indeed.
So, how long have you been a prostitute?

14:56.729 --> 14:59.459
No, Doug, I will not lift up her shirt.

14:59.565 --> 15:01.226
Chris, we have company.

15:01.333 --> 15:03.733
So, you ever been with a woman?

15:04.103 --> 15:05.195
No.

15:05.304 --> 15:06.635
- Peter!
- What?

15:07.273 --> 15:09.468
There. Are you happy, Doug?

15:10.409 --> 15:13.207
Christopher Cross Griffin,
what are you doing?

15:13.312 --> 15:15.177
Joe, what are you doing here?

15:15.281 --> 15:19.843
Peter, we have proof that it was Chris
who vandalized Goldman's Pharmacy.

15:19.952 --> 15:24.116
I knew it.
I didn't want to believe it, but it's true.

15:24.223 --> 15:27.386
Oh, God, what happened to my baby.

15:27.493 --> 15:28.892
Who sold you the drugs?

15:28.994 --> 15:30.518
I can't believe this!

15:31.463 --> 15:32.760
[AII arguing]

15:40.639 --> 15:43.130
...what a cavity search is.

15:45.577 --> 15:47.772
You made my mom cry tonight, Doug.

15:47.880 --> 15:50.178
I don't think you're a very good friend.

15:50.282 --> 15:52.375
I am not gonna listen to you anymore.

15:52.484 --> 15:55.385
Oh, yeah? I'm inside your head now, fatty.

15:55.487 --> 15:58.217
And I just might reach into your brain
and do this.

15:58.490 --> 16:00.822
Okay, I'll listen.

16:00.993 --> 16:01.982
[Laughing]

16:02.094 --> 16:03.254
That's my boy.

16:03.362 --> 16:06.456
Now, grab my bacon grease
and slather me up some homeys.

16:09.368 --> 16:11.302
- What's going on, man?
- Wassup, dog.

16:11.403 --> 16:13.462
Yeah, where are all the whiteheads at?

16:17.309 --> 16:21.336
Brian, we've had some wonderful times.
I really like you.

16:21.447 --> 16:23.711
Look, I understand. It's okay.

16:23.816 --> 16:26.649
I hope you and Quagmire
have all the happiness in the world.

16:26.752 --> 16:27.878
But I am choosing you.

16:27.987 --> 16:30.421
Just promise me
you'll make him wear this... What?

16:30.522 --> 16:33.923
You're choosing me?
After what happened with my family?

16:34.026 --> 16:37.553
Well, it wasn't as bad as the evening
I spent with Glenn and his mother.

16:40.199 --> 16:41.996
Glenn, would you feed Mittens?

16:42.101 --> 16:43.500
Mittens has food in his bowl.

16:43.602 --> 16:45.399
That's old food!

16:45.504 --> 16:47.438
Mittens, shut up!

16:47.539 --> 16:50.975
Don't you talk to Mittens that way.
Mittens is a member of this family.

16:51.076 --> 16:54.603
Mom, you want this three-way to happen,
you're gonna have to change your tone.

16:54.847 --> 16:58.248
My God, you've just made me
the happiest dog in the world.

16:58.350 --> 17:01.251
- I love you, Brooke.
- I love you, too, Brian.

17:06.425 --> 17:08.416
All right, that's a wrap.

17:09.395 --> 17:12.159
Well, it was great working with you, Brian.
Good luck.

17:12.431 --> 17:15.696
What are you talking about?
What about us?

17:15.801 --> 17:17.928
Oh, stop it. It's just TV.

17:21.206 --> 17:23.037
- Hi, Brian.
- Michael Eisner?

17:23.142 --> 17:26.168
On behalf of ABC,
I'd like to give you this parting gift.

17:26.278 --> 17:27.506
A bill for the mansion.

17:27.613 --> 17:29.547
No givesies-backsies!

17:35.387 --> 17:37.821
Hey, Brooke, it's me again, Brian.

17:38.090 --> 17:41.719
Hi. Wasn't sure
if you got my last message...

17:42.194 --> 17:45.891
or any of the other ones.
Anyway, I'll just leave a quick message...

17:45.998 --> 17:48.193
'cause you might be trying
to call me right now.

17:48.300 --> 17:51.565
And I don't want to tie up the line.
So, I guess...

17:51.670 --> 17:54.161
I guess... Yeah, give me a call.

17:55.174 --> 17:56.937
Okay, I'm hanging up...

17:57.042 --> 18:00.307
in three, two, one.

18:00.712 --> 18:02.202
Okay, call me back.

18:02.314 --> 18:05.841
I'll be here all day, and tonight.

18:06.218 --> 18:07.549
Okay, bye.

18:10.823 --> 18:14.452
Hey, me again. Thought I might've
heard a voice when I was hanging up.

18:14.560 --> 18:17.586
Nope? I guess not.
Okay, I will talk to you soon.

18:17.796 --> 18:19.457
Hello? No. Sorry.

18:22.000 --> 18:23.991
Hey, babe. Just trying you again.

18:24.103 --> 18:28.096
Listening to our guy Coltrane,
you know. Okay.

18:28.207 --> 18:32.166
Anyway, I got a fax earlier
about cheap airfare to Cancun.

18:32.277 --> 18:35.303
Didn't know if that was you
trying to reach me.

18:35.747 --> 18:38.580
Let me give you my home number again
just in case you lost it.

18:38.684 --> 18:40.879
<i>- Voicemail is full.
- Damn.</i>

18:40.986 --> 18:41.953
[Doorbell ringing]

18:42.988 --> 18:46.082
- Package for Brooke Roberts.
- Oh, that's me. Thanks.

18:47.826 --> 18:49.589
<i>BRIAN: Hey, there. Me again.</i>

18:49.695 --> 18:53.426
<i>Your voicemail was full,
so I got you this answering machine.</i>

18:53.532 --> 18:56.626
<i>So, what's going on?</i>

18:56.735 --> 18:59.465
<i>I was thinking about
doing something tonight...</i>

18:59.571 --> 19:00.765
Hey, you're home.

19:01.807 --> 19:06.039
Listen, Brian, I want you
to leave me alone, or I'm calling the cops.

19:07.179 --> 19:11.275
<i>[Singing] Brooke, I'm so in love with you</i>

19:20.959 --> 19:22.483
Chris, where the hell are we?

19:22.594 --> 19:25.825
I told you, Doug, this is the bacon factory.

19:26.265 --> 19:28.563
Doctor, I need you to get rid of this zit.

19:28.667 --> 19:31.261
- You traitor!
- That's a doozy.

19:31.370 --> 19:34.066
I bet some of those awful kids at school
call you zit-face.

19:34.173 --> 19:35.140
- No.
- Pop-a-zit.

19:35.240 --> 19:36.207
- No.
- Puspeak.

19:36.308 --> 19:37.275
- No.
- Fat ass?

19:37.376 --> 19:39.276
- Yeah.
- That's terrible.

19:39.378 --> 19:41.471
We're gonna have to use
some cortisone on that.

19:41.580 --> 19:43.946
Oh, yeah? Two can play at that game.

19:45.517 --> 19:47.314
Don't think I won't do it, man.

19:47.419 --> 19:49.785
All right, let's all be cool here.

19:59.831 --> 20:01.264
No!

20:03.902 --> 20:05.096
You okay, fat ass?

20:07.806 --> 20:11.970
She told me she loved me
on what used to be a hit TV show.

20:12.077 --> 20:15.205
I can't believe I got sucked into
that phony reality world...

20:15.314 --> 20:18.545
just like everyone else.
I became the very thing I was mocking.

20:18.650 --> 20:21.517
I know it hurts now, Brian,
but look at the bright side.

20:21.620 --> 20:24.646
You have some new material
for that novel you've been writing.

20:24.756 --> 20:27.554
You know, the novel
you've been working on.

20:28.026 --> 20:31.587
You know, the one
you've been working on for three years.

20:31.897 --> 20:33.626
You know, the novel.

20:34.199 --> 20:37.032
You got something new
to write about now, you know.

20:37.135 --> 20:41.037
Maybe a main character
gets into a relationship...

20:41.740 --> 20:44.140
then suffers a little heartbreak.

20:44.243 --> 20:47.474
Something like
what you've just been through.

20:47.713 --> 20:49.943
Draw from a real-life experience.

20:50.649 --> 20:54.278
Little heartbreak, you know,
work it into the story.

20:54.920 --> 20:58.321
Make those characters
a little more three-dimensional.

20:58.423 --> 21:01.256
A little richer experience for the reader.

21:01.493 --> 21:03.757
Make those second hundred pages...

21:03.862 --> 21:06.524
really keep the reader guessing
what's going to happen.

21:06.632 --> 21:09.226
Some twists and turns. Little epilogue.

21:10.035 --> 21:12.868
Everybody learns the hero's journey
isn't always a happy one.

21:12.971 --> 21:14.666
Yeah, I look forward to reading it.

21:14.667 --> 22:15.667
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru